<p dir="auto">The Description section of <code class="notranslate">Temporal.ZonedDateTime.prototype.add()</code> claimed that offset-ambiguous results use <code class="notranslate">offset: "prefer"</code>, but the spec's AddZonedDateTime algorithm uses <code class="notranslate">disambiguation: "compatible"</code> — the same mechanism as the date-time validity bullet directly above.</p>
<p dir="auto">Also fixes the second example: subtracting one day from <code class="notranslate">2024-11-04T01:00:00-05:00[America/New_York]</code> yields <code class="notranslate">2024-11-03T01:00:00-04:00[America/New_York]</code> (offset -04:00, not -05:00 as previously stated).</p>]]></content>
